error: a method declares exactly one role — this one declares `#[mutation]` and `#[entity]`. Accepted: `#[query]`, `#[mutation]`, `#[subscription]`, `#[entity]` or `#[field_resolver]`. Keeping the first and dropping the second would run the method under a role you did not write, so neither is assumed: a method that must be two is two methods. An entity resolver is a `Query`-root field — the router reaches it through `_entities`, which the `Mutation` and `Subscription` roots do not have.
